 "text": "Hello there! How's life treating you these days? Of course! That's tough situation, but not impossible. Do you want stick together as a unit, or split each getting one half each? Some restaurants keep a tally for you, or you can check the menus online. Splitting is neat if you end up doing the same things together. The basic ones to watch for are wheat, barley, oats, rye, in foods they're easy to spot, like wheat flour in bread and pasta, barley in beer and oats in porridge. Unfortunately, soy is a big one. It hiding under so many aliases, like tofu, tempeh, and soya milk. Fruit and most vegetables are gluten free, as are many condiments. True, but now you know for future trips. Let your friend get the special dish, and split everything else even. It's the fairest way.",
